    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABBBijbQ",
      "title": "Add Unichain mainnet PAO transition tasks (eth/069-070)",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1527,
      "body": "Transitions the Unichain Mainnet (chainId 130) ProxyAdmin Owner to the standard OP-governed model per the [governance post](https://app.notion.com/p/oplabs/EXTERNAL-Maintenance-Upgrade-Proposal-Unichain-ProxyAdmin-Owner-Transition-to-Standard-Optimism-Go-381f153ee16281efad21c307cef7c928): eth/069 transfers the L1 `ProxyAdmin` and `DisputeGameFactory` from the Unichain 3-of-3 to the standard L1PAO (`TransferOwners`), then eth/070 moves the L2 `ProxyAdmin` predeploy to the aliased L1PAO via a portal deposit sent by the 3-of-3 (`TransferL2PAOFromL1`). Same flow as eth/063/064 on Swell, signed by the 3-of-3's `chain-governor`/`foundation`/`council` child safes. Both tasks are DRAFT until the special voting cycle and veto period complete; all addresses are sourced from the superchain-registry (links in the task docs).\r\n\r\nEverything else on Unichain is already standard or out of scope: Guardian, Challenger and SuperchainConfig are the OP Mainnet ones, DelayedWETH is post-U16 and not ownable, and the SystemConfig owner stays with the operator per the governance post. Sepolia is covered by the same proposal but not part of this PR.\r\n\r\nTwo drive-bys: eth/065 is marked EXECUTED ([tx](https://etherscan.io/tx/0xbf75cc41981ecb8481f3b114697310490b72f96c74fcc34e33b57433b6d9e756)) — its stale READY-TO-SIGN status broke the eth stacked simulation — and `docs/simulate-l2-ownership-transfer.md` step 9 now shows the correct example `From` address.\r\n\r\nNote: the FUS/SC nonce pins overlap with #1521 (both stack after eth/066); whichever set of tasks signs second must re-pin and re-simulate.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-26T03:25:55Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 533,
      "deletions": 1
